# File: tests/bdd/features/audio_component.feature
# Generated from: specs/237-scaffold-an-audio-system-component-that-plays-imported-sounds-by-name-and-refresh-its-table-after-import-audio/requirements.md
Feature: Audio system component with a refreshed sound table

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Scaffold creates an Audio component
    Given a system entry "Audio" with template "audio" in the backlog
    When design scaffold runs
    Then "game/systems/Audio/audio.gd" declares "extends NmgAudio" and loads "res://systems/Audio/audio_table.tres"
    And "game/systems/Audio/audio_table.tres" is an NmgAudioTable resource

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Existing systems are unchanged
    Given a system entry "Inventory" without template and an existing "game/systems/Audio/audio.gd"
    When design scaffold runs
    Then "game/systems/Inventory/inventory.gd" extends Node
    And the existing Audio script is reported unchanged and not rewritten

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Refresh fills the name table
    Given "game/assets/Audio/PunchLight.wav", "game/assets/Audio/ForestTheme.ogg", and region "Forest" with music "ForestTheme"
    When python -m nmg_game_dev.audio refresh runs twice
    Then the table maps "PunchLight" and "ForestTheme" to their res:// paths and theme "Forest" to "ForestTheme"
    And the second run leaves the table byte-identical

  @SCN004
  Scenario: import_audio refreshes automatically
    Given a project with an Audio component table
    When import_audio imports sound effect "DoorCreak"
    Then the table maps "DoorCreak" to "res://assets/Audio/DoorCreak.wav"
    And the result's refreshed_tables lists the table

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Calling a missing sound is safe
    Given an NmgAudio whose table has no sound "NotYetImported"
    When sfx("NotYetImported", Vector3(1, 0, 0)) is called twice
    Then nothing plays and exactly one warning names "NotYetImported"

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Music crossfades, loops, and ducks for stingers
    Given an NmgAudio playing music "A"
    When music("A") is called again, then music("B"), then stinger("S")
    Then "A" keeps its player on the repeat call
    And "A" stops while "B" plays and replays when it finishes
    And the music is lowered by duck_db until "S" finishes

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Volumes persist
    Given set_volumes(0.8, 0.5, 1.0) was called
    When a new NmgAudio with the same settings path enters the tree
    Then its volumes are 0.8, 0.5, and 1.0

  @SCN008
  Scenario: The flow and fields are documented
    Given the ElevenLabs, design contract, and finalize MCP docs
    When a reader looks up the audio component
    Then they describe scaffold, import, refresh, and gameplay calls, the template and music fields, and refresh_audio_table

  @SCN009
  Scenario: Sync validates the new fields
    Given a system entry with template "lights" and a region entry with an empty music value
    When design sync runs
    Then it reports design.invalid_field for "template" and for "music"
